Great question! Your code is actually doing exactly what you told it to. Look at your indentation: the `break` statement is inside the for loop, which means it executes during the first iteration. So the loop prints 0, then immediately breaks and exits. If you want to print all numbers 0-9, simply remove the `break` statement or move it outside the loop by dedenting it: 

for i in range(10):
    print(i)

This way, `print(i)` runs for each value of i (0 through 9) without any interruption. The `break` statement is useful when you want to exit a loop early based on a condition, like:

for i in range(10):
    print(i)
    if i == 5:
        break

This would print 0-5 and then stop. Try removing break from your original code and see what happens!
